# apps/kingdom-tactics-server

The Kingdom Tactics multiplayer server (Phase 4). An Express 5 + `ws` Node app that mirrors
`apps/game-server`'s bootstrap (`@shatteredarchive/services-server`: `getConfigFromEnv` +
`createExpressService`, Winston logging, `/health`) and mounts a `/ws/kt` WebSocket gateway
hosting **server-authoritative** matches.

Architecture: all game rules AND match ownership live in `@shatteredarchive/kingdom-tactics-engine`
(`MatchSession`, isomorphic — this app never reimplements it); this app is transport +
match-lifecycle glue only. `MatchSession` owns a `GameEngine`/`MatchState` per match, authorizes
each client action (seat ownership + engine legality), and auto-plays an `IAiPolicy`
(GreedyPolicy) opponent. `src/ws/kt-gateway` mounts the socket, keeps a `MatchRegistry`
(matchId → session + subscribers), validates untrusted frames against the engine's shared
`net/protocol` contract, and broadcasts full-state snapshots (v1: no deltas). Default port 51000.
No reconnect yet.

**Phase F (centralized auth) — join-frame auth added.** A `join` frame's optional `token` is
introspected via `@shatteredarchive/services-server`'s `introspect`/`matchesAudience`
(`index.ts`'s `buildAccountIdResolver`, wired as `setupKtWebSocketGateway`'s `resolveAccountId`)
and, on success, attached to the claimed seat as an accountId (`MatchSession.claimSeat`'s
optional 3rd arg, read via `claimedSeats()` — pure metadata, never consulted by seat-ownership
authorization itself). Additive only: no token, an invalid/expired token, or an unreachable
auth-server all resolve to the SAME outcome as before this phase — a fully anonymous join, never
a rejection. This service holds its own registered Ed25519 key (a STANDARD Phase A consumer,
unlike game-client's Phase D pattern of borrowing another service's key — kingdom-tactics-server
is a real backend and performs its own SSO code exchange).

**Phase F — persistence + this service's first-ever HTTP surface beyond `/`/`/health`.**
`src/persistence/` holds two per-account JSON file stores (`src/persistence/json-account-store.ts`'s
generic `<dataDir>/<subdir>/<accountId>.json` helper): `MatchHistoryStore` (25-entry cap, oldest
evicted; a no-op for a fully-anonymous match) and `ArmyLayoutStore` (100-army cap, mirrors
kt-client's `state/saved-armies.ts` shape exactly). `MatchSession` gained action-log accumulation
+ `replaySeed()`/`initial()` + `replayAction()` (Phase F, in the engine) so a completed match can
be deterministically reconstructed later via `replayMatch` — the hidden-outcome `combatSalt`
never leaves the server (`match-history/:id/replay` runs the replay server-side and returns only
the resulting state sequence). `setupKtWebSocketGateway`'s new `onMatchComplete` hook (guarded by
`MatchSession.tryClaimForRecording()` for an exactly-once fire) is where `index.ts` wires a
finished match into `MatchHistoryStore.record()`. `src/http/kt-api-routes.ts` adds
`GET /api/kt/match-history`, `GET /api/kt/match-history/:id/replay`, and
`GET`/`PUT /api/kt/army-layouts`, all guarded by `src/http/auth-guard.ts`'s `requireAccount` — a
DIFFERENT failure policy than the WS join resolver: these routes 401 on a missing/invalid token
rather than degrading to anonymous, since "my match history" has no anonymous equivalent.

**Phase F Step 3 — kt-client's login hand-off.** `src/http/kt-sso-routes.ts` adds
`GET /api/kt/auth/start` (validates `returnUrl`'s origin against `KT_CLIENT_ALLOWED_RETURN_ORIGINS`,
sets a `kt-sso-state` cookie — hand-rolled, no `cookie-parser` dependency added for one narrow
use — redirects to the hub's `/sso/authorize`) and `GET /api/kt/auth/callback` (validates state,
exchanges the code via `services-server`'s `exchangeCode` — injected as a dependency so this
file's own test suite never imports `services-server` at all, sidestepping a real transitive
ESM-parse issue in this app's jest config; ANY future file needing `services-server` in a test
should do the same, not chase that rabbit hole again — redirects to kt-client with
`#auth_token=...&expires_at=...`, same safe fragment mechanism as game-client's Phase D). Only
registered when this service is actually configured for it (missing credentials/allowlist ⇒ a
clear 404 on "log in," never a half-working flow). `index.ts` builds `readServiceCredentials`
ONCE, shared by the WS resolver, the `/api/kt/*` HTTP guard, AND these SSO routes. The
`hubBaseUrl` used for both the browser redirect and the exchange is the SAME public edge URL
today (this service isn't dockerized yet) — Step 4's dockerization should split this into a
public-vs-internal pair like the C# site's `AuthorizeBaseUrl`/`BaseUrl`, not before.
